    "ESCALATION_STATUS": {
        "_comment": [
            "Escalation state. This concept already existed in mappings.json and",
            "in capability_evidence_patterns.json, but had no entry here, and",
            "SemanticInference scores a column only against patterns present in",
            "this file. The concept was therefore unreachable from the main",
            "mapping pass and any finding citing it was untraceable there.",
            "",
            "The keyword and category sets mirror the capability pattern file so",
            "the two passes select the same columns and the only change is which",
            "pass is reported as the source. The time/date/duration negatives are",
            "the same guard SECURITY_SEVERITY already uses, and _by is the actor",
            "guard: an escalation performed BY someone is not an escalation",
            "state. These are needed in pairs because the scorer adds +0.25 per",
            "matching negative keyword but caps the total penalty at 0.5, so a",
            "single match (-0.25) cannot pull a keyword hit below the 0.45",
            "threshold once the category bonus is added back."
        ],
        "keywords": [
            "escalation",
            "escalated",
            "escalation_status",
            "escalation_state",
            "escalation_level",
            "escalation_required",
            "is_escalated",
            "escalation_reason"
        ],
        "negative_keywords": [
            "escalation_time",
            "escalated_by",
            "_by",
            "time",
            "date",
            "duration"
        ],
        "expected_categories": [
            "categorical",
            "identifier_like",
            "numeric"
        ]
    },
    "ASSET_CRITICALITY": {
        "_comment": [
            "Asset/system criticality: how important the ASSET is. This is a",
            "different axis from SECURITY_SEVERITY (how severe the ALERT is) and",
            "the two must never resolve to the same concept.",
            "",
            "Keywords are deliberately asset-qualified. A bare 'criticality'",
            "keyword is what previously let asset_criticality resolve to",
            "SECURITY_SEVERITY, so it is NOT used here either: 'criticality' alone",
            "does not say whether the criticality belongs to the asset or to the",
            "alert, and 'alert_criticality' is severity evidence, not asset",
            "evidence. The negative keywords push alert-shaped names away.",
            "",
            "Like SECURITY_SEVERITY, this concept declares no value_patterns: the",
            "scorer adds +0.25 per matching value pattern, so value agreement is",
            "left to category confirmation rather than used to admit a column on",
            "its values alone."
        ],
        "keywords": [
            "asset_criticality",
            "asset_critical",
            "asset_importance",
            "system_criticality",
            "device_criticality",
            "business_impact"
        ],
        "negative_keywords": [
            "alert",
            "severity",
            "priority",
            "escalation",
            "time",
            "date",
            "duration",
            "user",
            "owner",
            "closed_by"
        ],
        "expected_categories": [
            "categorical",
            "numeric",
            "identifier_like"
        ]
    },
